---
description: pi-tinker development and Tinker/Inkling workflow rules
alwaysApply: true
---

Read `AGENTS.md` and `docs/coding-agents.md` before making changes.

Pi is the primary interactive interface. In Cursor's shell, invoke the same command workflow with:

```bash
node scripts/agent-cli.mjs <tinker-subcommand> [options]
```

Use official Tinker SDK, Tinker Cookbook, and `tml-renderers`. Keep generated Python editable and do not build a parallel training abstraction. Default to `thinkingmachines/Inkling` while preserving explicit alternative-model support. Keep baseline/checkpoint effort matched and require user approval before API-using eval or training stages.
